      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To save the bill, you must frame 'Tier 2 Compliance' as the essential guardrail that filters out low-quality, unreliable global competitors, thereby ensuring the long-term viability and security of U.S. supply chains for all voters. By positioning this clause as a strategic assertion of domestic benefit rather than a cost, you shift the narrative from financial burden to economic fortification and national self-sufficiency. This reframing suggests that the bill protects American workers and infrastructure by demanding a higher standard of quality, which ultimately drives better domestic production that foreign rivals simply cannot match regardless of their initial subsidies.",
