      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can pre-empt his question by framing the short-term margin \"squeezes\" as an inevitable but temporary investment in long-term operational excellence and real productivity gains before the Capital efficiency kicks in. Acknowledge the initial adjustment period honestly but pivot immediately to the permanent structural improvement that will actually lower total costs and improve global competitiveness in the second year. This approach validates his concern for the present while confidently asserting that the bill's long-term strategic benefits far outweigh the immediate transition costs.\n</think>\n\nYou can pre-empt his question by framing the short-term margin \"squeezes\" as an inevitable but temporary investment in long-term operational excellence and real productivity gains before the capital efficiency kicks in. Acknowledge the adjustment period honestly but pivot immediately to the permanent structural improvement that will actually lower total costs and improve global competitiveness in the second year. This approach validates his concern for the present while confidently asserting that the bill's long-term strategic benefits far outweigh the immediate transition costs.",
